    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression $1+6\\cdot2-3+5\\cdot4\\div2$, we need to follow the order of operations (PEMDAS/BODMAS). This stands for Parentheses/Brackets, Exponents/Orders, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), and Addition and Subtraction (from left to right).\n\nLet's break down the expression step by step:\n\n1. First, we have $6\\cdot2$. According to the order of operations, we should perform this multiplication first.\n\\[\n6\\cdot2 = 12\n\\]\nNow, our expression looks like this:\n\\[\n1+12-3+5\\cdot4\\div2\n\\]\n\n2. Next, we perform the division $5\\cdot4\\div2$. Division is also at the multiplication and division level, so we should perform this next.\n\\[\n5\\cdot4\\div2 = (5\\cdot4)\\div2 = 20\\div2 = 10\n\\]\nNow, our expression is:\n\\[\n1+12-3+10\n\\]\n\n3. Next, we perform addition and subtraction from left to right.\n\\[\n1+12 = 13\n\\]\nNow, our expression is:\n\\[\n13-3+10\n\\]\n\n\\[\n13-3 = 10\n\\]\n\nSo, $10+10 = 20$.\n\nLet's verify this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculating the expression step by step using Python\n\n# Initial expression\nexpression_result = 1 + 6 * 2 - 3 + 5 * 4 / 2\n\nprint(expression_result)\n```\n```output\n20.0\n```\nThe final answer to the expression $1+6\\cdot2-3+5\\cdot4\\div2$ is \\boxed{20}.",
